---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import MainPanelTabs from '../../components/MainPanelTabs.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Linking Manager">
  <h1>Main Panel — Linking Manager</h1>
  <MainPanelTabs activeTab="main-panel/linking-manager" />
  <p>
    The <strong>Linking Manager</strong> coordinates Blender's Light and Shadow Linking features. It bypasses the tedious process of manually dragging collections inside property panels by rendering simple column tags and popups next to each active light.
  </p>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 1. Light Linking ──</h2>
  <p>
    Restrict which objects receive light from a specific emitter:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs mb-6">
    <li><strong>Receiver Collections:</strong> Assign light illumination exclusively to chosen collections.</li>
    <li><strong>Real-time Highlighting:</strong> The viewport draws colored wireframes around receivers in real-time.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 2. Shadow Linking ──</h2>
  <p>
    Calibrate shadows by designating specific objects as shadow blockers:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-xs mb-6">
    <li><strong>Blocker Isolation:</strong> Exclude or include objects in a light's shadow path to clean up render aesthetics.</li>
    <li><strong>Visual feedback:</strong> Orange outlines indicate active shadow block parameters in the viewport.</li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>
